# The options FTC-Sim.cmd starts the Java runtime of this folder with: the format of a Java argument file, one option a line.
# They are also in the application's jar, where the self test checks that the running Java was given every one, and
# :app:run starts the application with them. Native access is for the window's libraries (Skia, LWJGL, Jolt); the
# memory access option keeps the JDK from warning about the sun.misc.Unsafe use of those libraries and of the FTC SDK.
--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED
--sun-misc-unsafe-memory-access=allow
